cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Carrying an ECG-AI threshold from inpatients to outpatients: a retrospective measurement of three structural heart disease models in one hospital system"
message: If you use this repository, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Abbou
    given-names: Ruben
repository-code: https://github.com/rabbou/ecg-conformal-shift
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-30
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  At Columbia, a threshold set to catch 90% of inpatients with moderate or
  worse structural heart disease caught {{sens_resnet_out}} of outpatients with
  it for a network trained on EchoNext, {{sens_mini_out}} for the published
  EchoNext mini-model and {{sens_ecgf_out}} for ECGFounder, while the AUROC
  moved from {{auroc_resnet_in}} to {{auroc_resnet_out}} for the trained network. Set
  again on 100 outpatients with known diagnoses, the threshold caught
  {{lad100_sens_resnet}} of the other outpatients' ill on average and flagged
  {{lad100_hflag_resnet}} of 100 healthy; set on {{vo_n}} separate outpatients, it
  caught {{vo_sens_resnet}}, {{vo_sens_mini}} and {{vo_sens_ecgf}}, short of 90% for
  all three models. An infarction
  model carried from PTB-XL to hospitals in Chongqing and Shandong is reported
  beside it, with a rotation of five public corpora on five rhythm and
  conduction diagnoses.
keywords:
  - electrocardiography
  - structural heart disease
  - decision threshold
  - sensitivity
  - spectrum effect
  - distribution shift
